sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-11: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.30";
    dc:description "Within-bot consistency is measurable from the same five-hour tracks as the transition matrix, and those tracks are not public. Even with them, rare switching would not show that bots self-organize into types rather than simply keeping the geometry they had when recording started. The stability half is waiting on data; the self-organization wording stays underdetermined.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For each bot, compute the fraction of its 30-second segments that stay in one movement class and the rate of switches between circular and linear. High within-bot consistency and rare cross-class switches would support stable individual types; frequent switching by the same bot would refute a lasting fingerprint. Separating active self-organization from a type fixed by the initial cilia pattern needs early-time tracks the consistency score alone does not provide.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A fingerprint is only as discrete as the upstream cluster boundaries.", "Low switching does not distinguish self-organization from a type fixed at release by cilia geometry.", "Per-bot identity of segments is not in a public file.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.66"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.297"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2024-anthrobots-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.18";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.18"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok--data-adequacy> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
